1
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:47,959
Mentor.

2
00:01:48,799 --> 00:01:50,959
You don't think Ding Ning passed out, do you?

3
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:52,680
What normal person sleeps from the morning

4
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:53,840
all the way to the afternoon?

5
00:01:53,879 --> 00:01:55,319
Why didn't you call an ambulance?

6
00:01:58,599 --> 00:02:00,079
Did that male caregiver's girlfriend

7
00:02:00,079 --> 00:02:01,239
reply to your messages?

8
00:02:01,239 --> 00:02:02,040
No.

9
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,239
Did she reply to you?

10
00:02:03,719 --> 00:02:04,680
What if they bail on us?

11
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,200
Who are we going to ask for the legal fees?

12
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,000
Why are you still hanging around here?

13
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:09,439
Didn't I assign you a new job?

14
00:02:09,439 --> 00:02:11,879
Don't be in a rush to kick me out. I'm almost done.

15
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:13,639
You're awake.

16
00:02:16,759 --> 00:02:17,960
I found that witness.

17
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:19,120
Ding Ning, let me tell you.

18
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:20,240
Based on the current situation,

19
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:22,599
it doesn't mean you'll get an acquittal.

20
00:02:23,879 --> 00:02:25,039
We need to discredit the testimony that

21
00:02:25,039 --> 00:02:26,960
Zhang Lin abused the old and young. I know.

22
00:02:27,639 --> 00:02:29,400
Even though a cellmate's testimony

23
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:30,479
is considered hearsay evidence

24
00:02:30,479 --> 00:02:32,120
and might not be accepted by the court,

25
00:02:32,199 --> 00:02:33,759
we still need to investigate it thoroughly.

26
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:34,759
After all, it could influence

27
00:02:34,759 --> 00:02:36,479
the judge's own judgment later on,

28
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:38,759
and the probative value of other evidence.

29
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:41,240
I've already investigated it.

30
00:02:41,319 --> 00:02:42,439
It's a hornet's nest.

31
00:02:42,439 --> 00:02:43,759
I advise you not to touch it.

32
00:02:44,159 --> 00:02:45,680
If you want to help that male caregiver,

33
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,000
you have to handle this witness.

34
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,680
It means getting involved in a drug trafficking case.

35
00:02:49,439 --> 00:02:50,360
Can you even touch that?

36
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:53,159
A drug trafficking case?

37
00:02:54,319 --> 00:02:55,599
What's wrong with a drug trafficking case?

38
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:57,400
Why can't Ding Ning handle it?

39
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,319
Because not touching drug cases

40
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,719
was the condition for me to be allowed to practice law.

41
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,520
Ding Kuihai has a comrade's son named Fan Dong.

42
00:03:13,719 --> 00:03:15,120
Fan Dong was celebrating his birthday at my house,

43
00:03:15,479 --> 00:03:16,479
but he still couldn't escape

44
00:03:16,479 --> 00:03:18,680
the drug dealers' secret birthday gift.

45
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:22,479
Fan Dong's father's body parts.

46
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,000
His father was an undercover narcotics cop.

47
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,000
Freeze!

48
00:03:27,319 --> 00:03:28,719
After his cover was blown,

49
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,199
he was murdered by the drug dealers in retaliation.

50
00:03:31,199 --> 00:03:31,879
After that, Fan Dong's family

51
00:03:31,879 --> 00:03:33,800
would receive body parts every now and then.

52
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:35,680
His grandmother, overwhelmed with grief,

53
00:03:35,719 --> 00:03:37,000
fell ill and died shortly after.

54
00:03:39,639 --> 00:03:41,080
Ding Kuihai took Fan Dong in

55
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,000
and raised him as his own son.

56
00:03:43,479 --> 00:03:44,560
Five years flew by.

57
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,039
Every meal was torture for him.

58
00:03:47,759 --> 00:03:49,800
Because Fan Dong couldn't stand chopped meat.

59
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:50,919
Anything that could remind him

60
00:03:50,919 --> 00:03:52,479
of his father's body parts

61
00:03:52,479 --> 00:03:54,360
would trigger massive panic in him.

62
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:55,439
Fan Dong!

63
00:03:55,439 --> 00:03:57,159
It must have been from that moment on

64
00:03:57,479 --> 00:03:57,879
that Ding Kuihai

65
00:03:57,879 --> 00:03:59,520
decided to do whatever it takes,

66
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,680
to make the drug dealers pay in blood.

67
00:04:02,319 --> 00:04:04,400
He volunteered to join the narcotics brigade.

68
00:04:04,719 --> 00:04:06,159
No matter how stubborn the drug dealers were,

69
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:07,520
he could always make them talk.

70
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:08,639
Are you gonna talk? I'll talk! I'll talk!

71
00:04:08,879 --> 00:04:10,360
Later, a habitual thief

72
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:12,159
was tortured to death by his subordinates.

73
00:04:12,759 --> 00:04:14,000
The family escalated the matter to the provincial level.

74
00:04:14,159 --> 00:04:15,520
Ding Kuihai bore joint responsibility

75
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:16,720
and was dismissed and investigated.

76
00:04:16,959 --> 00:04:17,759
After that,

77
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:21,240
Ding Kuihai officially became my stepfather.

78
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:23,600
A father who kidnapped and murdered,

79
00:04:24,319 --> 00:04:26,199
a stepfather who tortured for confessions,

80
00:04:26,399 --> 00:04:27,279
and a childhood friend who received

81
00:04:27,279 --> 00:04:29,000
his own father's dismembered body parts.

82
00:04:29,439 --> 00:04:31,240
How on earth did you grow up?

83
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:44,720
My girl is back.

84
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,240
Ningning, Fan Dong is cooking today.

85
00:04:46,319 --> 00:04:48,040
Ding Ning, wash your hands and eat.

86
00:04:48,079 --> 00:04:49,439
Come, come, come.

87
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:51,040
Come on, come sit down and eat.

88
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:53,800
My girl is a top lawyer now.

89
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,240
She specializes in punishing scumbags.

90
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:57,360
Murderers must die.

91
00:04:57,519 --> 00:04:59,199
Drug dealers especially must die.

92
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:03,000
Those bastards who commit crimes...

93
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:04,319
...deserve a horrible death.

94
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:06,480
I don't care that I got fired.

95
00:05:06,519 --> 00:05:07,279
But...

96
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:09,879
if I could take those bastards down with me,

97
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:13,439
I wouldn't even blink.

98
00:05:13,759 --> 00:05:16,000
Come on, eat up and drink well.

99
00:05:17,319 --> 00:05:18,120
You're back.

100
00:05:19,639 --> 00:05:20,480
Been back for a while.

101
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:25,759
You cooked this?

102
00:05:26,639 --> 00:05:27,800
I specifically learned a few new recipes...

103
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:28,720
...for Mom and Dad to try.

104
00:05:31,519 --> 00:05:32,519
You're different now.

105
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:35,240
Well, we can't stay stuck in the past, can we?

106
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:36,759
We all have to look forward.

107
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:39,800
I'll head over first, then.

108
00:05:40,639 --> 00:05:41,720
Wash your hands. Hurry up.

109
00:05:51,959 --> 00:05:52,439
Hello?

110
00:05:52,439 --> 00:05:53,120
Ding Ning.

111
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:54,800
Anyway,

112
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:57,040
I'm heading to Rujie Law Firm tomorrow.

113
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:58,959
They originally wanted to send me

114
00:05:58,959 --> 00:05:59,959
to Rongshan County

115
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,279
to run a small errand.

116
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:04,240
I'll help investigate the drug dealers,

117
00:06:05,319 --> 00:06:06,560
and you go to Rongshan for me?

118
00:06:07,519 --> 00:06:08,240
Deal.

119
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:12,600
Thank you, Zhou Hao.

120
00:06:40,199 --> 00:06:40,920
Hello.

121
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:41,800
What is it?

122
00:06:43,399 --> 00:06:44,920
Are you guys closed for good?

123
00:06:45,959 --> 00:06:48,639
How can we be open? The boss took off.

124
00:06:48,639 --> 00:06:49,279
Excuse me.

125
00:06:49,279 --> 00:06:51,439
I really need to double-check with you.

126
00:06:51,639 --> 00:06:52,879
That night, I remember...

127
00:06:52,879 --> 00:06:54,079
Stop coming here.

128
00:06:54,079 --> 00:06:55,759
Weren't you just here a couple of days ago?

129
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:57,120
I already told you.

130
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:58,839
It was just you that day.

131
00:06:58,839 --> 00:06:59,839
You saw the security footage too.

132
00:06:59,839 --> 00:07:00,680
What do you want?

133
00:07:01,639 --> 00:07:02,959
Are you out of your mind?

134
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:05,319
Seriously.

135
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:24,920
Hello.

136
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:26,839
The number you have dialed is powered off.

137
00:07:26,839 --> 00:07:27,399
Sorry.

138
00:07:27,399 --> 00:07:28,800
The number you have dialed is powered off.

139
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:44,920
Senior.

140
00:07:48,959 --> 00:07:49,839
How have you been?

141
00:07:53,079 --> 00:07:53,920
I'm glad you're here.

142
00:07:54,839 --> 00:07:56,879
We've made a major breakthrough in our case.

143
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,040
There's an issue with the prosecution's evidence.

144
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:00,800
Now we just need that witness

145
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,079
who shared a cell with your boyfriend.

146
00:08:02,639 --> 00:08:03,759
Once we verify whether his testimony...

147
00:08:03,759 --> 00:08:05,279
Ding Ning, hold on a second.

148
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:07,079
Let her speak first.

149
00:08:07,519 --> 00:08:08,160
Go ahead.

150
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:09,879
Say what?

151
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:11,959
Is it about the legal fees?

152
00:08:12,759 --> 00:08:13,959
You don't have to worry about that.

153
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:15,560
I'm here for the case files.

154
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:17,680
According to regulations,

155
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:19,079
for a new lawyer to take the files,

156
00:08:19,279 --> 00:08:20,720
they need a consent letter from the court.

157
00:08:22,639 --> 00:08:23,519
Here are the authorization documents.

158
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:24,639
The court has already been notified.

159
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:27,560
I know what you're worried about.

160
00:08:27,759 --> 00:08:29,399
You're afraid even with a new judge,

161
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:30,879
the new judge or even the court

162
00:08:30,879 --> 00:08:32,080
will still be hostile toward me.

163
00:08:32,279 --> 00:08:33,519
But that's not how lawsuits work.

164
00:08:33,519 --> 00:08:35,120
Ding Ning, please stop talking.

165
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:36,279
Winning or losing a case

166
00:08:36,279 --> 00:08:37,639
doesn't depend on connections.

167
00:08:37,639 --> 00:08:39,320
Judges don't just favor those

168
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:40,159
they're on good terms with,

169
00:08:40,159 --> 00:08:41,480
or target those they dislike.

170
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:43,240
What matters is evidence, facts,

171
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:44,559
and the application of the law.

172
00:08:44,559 --> 00:08:45,000
Also...

173
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,159
But you didn't win.

174
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:49,120
You didn't win the first time.

175
00:08:49,519 --> 00:08:51,759
How can you guarantee you'll win this time?

176
00:08:51,759 --> 00:08:53,399
I'm just changing lawyers

177
00:08:53,639 --> 00:08:55,080
to ensure I win the next hearing,

178
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:56,120
so my man can get out.

179
00:08:56,440 --> 00:08:57,639
I can't wait any longer.

180
00:08:57,639 --> 00:08:59,039
My baby is already five months old.

181
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:00,720
Am I wrong?

182
00:09:01,039 --> 00:09:02,159
Haven't you ever considered

183
00:09:02,159 --> 00:09:03,320
how many people Ding Ning offended

184
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,120
lately just for your sake?

185
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,240
Alright, alright, stop talking.

186
00:09:07,159 --> 00:09:08,639
We really just need one witness's testimony,

187
00:09:08,639 --> 00:09:09,799
and we're set.

188
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:12,720
How about this?

189
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:14,320
I'll refund your money.

190
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:15,679
A criminal case

191
00:09:15,679 --> 00:09:17,559
can have two defense attorneys.

192
00:09:17,559 --> 00:09:19,120
I can work with the lawyer you hired

193
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:20,600
to co-represent this case.

194
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:21,720
Don't you think giving up so close to the end

195
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:22,879
is a real pity?

196
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:26,320
You can take them.

197
00:09:26,679 --> 00:09:28,240
Check carefully, make sure nothing is missing.

198
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,039
Okay.

199
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,159
Lao Yu.

200
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:57,720
Coming.

201
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:02,600
I brought some good food.

202
00:10:02,919 --> 00:10:04,000
Keep your shoes on.

203
00:10:06,799 --> 00:10:07,399
Okay.

204
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:10,519
Here.

205
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,720
It got sent back again.

206
00:10:20,799 --> 00:10:22,240
I just can't figure you out.

207
00:10:23,159 --> 00:10:24,399
You help just about anyone.

208
00:10:24,919 --> 00:10:27,799
You even forgive the people who hurt you.

209
00:10:28,159 --> 00:10:30,799
You don't care about money or power.

210
00:10:31,159 --> 00:10:32,879
And you avoid honors whenever you can.

211
00:10:33,360 --> 00:10:34,840
You don't smoke or drink.

212
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:36,440
You don't have a single bad habit.

213
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,039
You're so good, it's actually a bit scary.

214
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:44,200
Good thing I know you've been single all these years.

215
00:10:44,399 --> 00:10:46,000
Otherwise, I'd even suspect...

216
00:10:47,639 --> 00:10:49,039
that you and the guy in prison...

217
00:10:49,039 --> 00:10:50,279
might be accomplices.

218
00:10:50,759 --> 00:10:54,639
You're saying I hired Yang Cheng, right?

219
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:57,720
You watch way too many short videos.

220
00:10:58,440 --> 00:10:59,480
Conspiracy theories?

221
00:11:11,919 --> 00:11:13,320
What's in that folder

222
00:11:13,559 --> 00:11:14,879
is the information on the witness

223
00:11:14,879 --> 00:11:15,960
who might have framed the male caregiver.

224
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:17,960
You were right not to hand it over.

225
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,240
Don't let them guilt-trip you.

226
00:11:22,919 --> 00:11:24,960
Being a lawyer is just a way to make a living.

227
00:11:25,879 --> 00:11:27,120
Ending our partnership is fine.

228
00:11:27,679 --> 00:11:28,519
We owe each other nothing.

229
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,879
I hope that after this incident,

230
00:11:32,879 --> 00:11:33,679
you've learned a lesson.

231
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:34,840
What lesson?

232
00:11:35,679 --> 00:11:37,080
That I shouldn't have reported Yu Songfan?

233
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:38,919
Or that I shouldn't have respected my client's choice

234
00:11:38,919 --> 00:11:40,679
and stood on the side of truth to appeal for him?

235
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:46,600
Many don't believe you tried suicide by charcoal.

236
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:48,639
But I do.

237
00:11:50,799 --> 00:11:52,759
Even though you always act so happy,

238
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:53,879
I feel like your life

239
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:55,080
is actually pretty meaningless.

240
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:57,159
Quitting your job is a good thing.

241
00:11:57,799 --> 00:12:00,440
It's the perfect chance for you to start over.

242
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:02,480
If you see good food, eat it.

243
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,080
If there are nice places you haven't been to,

244
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:05,799
go visit them.

245
00:12:05,799 --> 00:12:06,840
And given your physical condition right now,

246
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:08,320
you seem to be doing just fine, right?

247
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:10,679
If you meet a nice girl

248
00:12:10,679 --> 00:12:12,120
who you can settle down with,

249
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,519
go after her.

250
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,159
Live a little more authentically.

251
00:12:16,519 --> 00:12:17,840
Don't be so dull.

252
00:12:19,559 --> 00:12:20,399
I won't nag you any longer.

253
00:12:21,039 --> 00:12:22,399
Take your time eating. I'm taking off.

254
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:31,559
Lao Yu.

255
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:35,639
If you weren't trying to commit suicide that night...

256
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:37,600
then what were you burning?

257
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:48,559
Lao Qiu.

258
00:12:54,919 --> 00:12:59,759
There are some things I no longer want to dwell on.

259
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,519
And I've decided to let them fade away.

260
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:08,360
Isn't that a good thing?

261
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:17,120
A good thing.

262
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:18,360
Alright, I'm heading out.

263
00:13:21,399 --> 00:13:23,399
Stop writing letters to Yang Cheng in prison.

264
00:13:23,399 --> 00:13:24,519
He was released on medical parole.

265
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Terminal liver cancer.

266
00:13:29,559 --> 00:13:31,159
Someone just brought a package in for you.

267
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:32,320
See you.

268
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:33,360
Okay, okay.

269
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:38,240
I heard from Zhou Hao

270
00:13:38,519 --> 00:13:40,919
that you're going to Rongshan County in his place.

271
00:13:42,159 --> 00:13:42,840
For three days.

272
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:49,840
Hand it over.

273
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:57,720
Mentor.

274
00:13:57,919 --> 00:13:59,480
I want to take this evidence

275
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:01,360
proving that guy is a habitual liar

276
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:02,519
to the drug dealer's lawyer.

277
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:04,519
We don't need it,

278
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:06,360
but maybe they can put it to good use.

279
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:07,480
It could save that drug dealer.

280
